<title>USA: CEA LAB Inc to sell Bahamas property.</title>
<headline>CEA LAB Inc to sell Bahamas property.</headline>
<dateline>WICHITA, Kan. 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>CEA LAB Inc said Monday it will sell a 75-acre beachfront property in the Bahamas to NABCO Inc in a deal worth $1.5 million.</p>
<p>Payment for the property on Andros Island will include $150,000 worth of restricted common shares of NABCO and a promissory note to be paid in full by 2007, CEA LAB said.</p>
<p>NABCO said it plans to look for a joint venture partner to develop a hotel, marina and casino on the property.</p>
<p>CEA LAB is a holding company with interests in communications, publishing, investment banking and gourmet coffee.</p>
<p>((-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
